Task: Continuous integration workflow, and its confirmation on the remote

What runs: the linter, the format check, the core test suite, the coverage
gate and the layer boundary check, each as its own step so a failure points at
one thing. All of them need only a plain Lua interpreter.

What deliberately does not run: the drawing application is never built. That
build costs tens of minutes and about a gigabyte, which would make the result
too slow to read. The tests that need the real runtime stay local and remain
part of the phase gate.

The formatter is pinned. An unpinned formatter rewrites code to match whatever
it released last and turns a branch red with nobody having touched it.

Confirmed green on the first remote run, and confirmed to be measuring the real
thing: the remote log shows the same numbers as the local run - 72 tests, 28
files linted clean, core coverage 100 percent across 6 files, boundary clean -
and the pinned formatter version in the log matches the recorded one.

Also confirmed it can fail. A throwaway branch carrying a deliberately broken
tree turned the run red, stopped at the broken step and left the later steps
unrun. The branch was removed afterwards. A gate only ever seen passing is not
known to be a gate.
